<title>ZIMBABWE: Lower sugar output hits Hippo Valley EPS.</title>
<headline>Lower sugar output hits Hippo Valley EPS.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>		 (million Zimbabwe dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		   70.8     vs   118.4</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		   28.0     vs    50.0</p>
<p>    Operating profit	 122.6     vs   251.4</p>
<p>    Interest received	 32.6     vs    48.2</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	   168.4     vs   310.4</p>
<p>    Tax			   32.3     vs    83.0</p>
<p>    After-tax profit	 136.1     vs   227.4</p>
<p>    Turnover		   705.1     vs   838.2</p>
<p>Div payable July 31</p>
<p>on register July 2</p>
<p>Full Name: Hippo Valley Estates Limited</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said the impact of a significant reduction in sugar production to 162,000 tonnes from 254,000 tonnes was reflected in the results for the year under review. However, the company had begun the current year in a strong position with water supplies assured until well after the next rainy season. It therefore looked forward to a return to satisfactory levels of earnings and dividends for the year to March 1998.</p>
<p>--Harare Newsroom: 263-4 72 52 27/8/9</p>
